 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? The chain is jumping on the big ring near the cassette. That's usually dirt or oil on the rear wheel. The chain comes off the big ring, turn the bike so the jump is on the left and the wheel is on the floor. Use a screwdriver to press the little metal tab in the gap of the chain on. Then it' dirt or oil. Spray the chain with a degreaser and wipe with rag, then dry it again.",
